-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Precision:** The use of a stop-gradient in the quantization function (Eq. 9 in source) prevents gradients from backpropagating during training, but this is a training-time detail. For baking, the primary precision concern is the threshold value. Setting the threshold too low may include occluded or noisy voxels, leading to artifacts; setting it too high may cull valid geometry. The value 0.005 is empirically chosen [S1].
-*   **Boundaries:** When marking the 8 surrounding voxels, care must be taken to ensure voxel coordinates are within the grid bounds [G].
-*   **Degenerate Input:** If the Proposal MLP fails to sample a region (e.g., completely occluded or out-of-bounds), those voxels will not be marked as occupied, which is the desired behavior for empty space skipping [S1].
